    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d980">

                <pb facs="0750" n="634" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg634"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14076.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Provisional President announces publicly today that he has had a very
                    satisfactory interview with General Villa and that the general will remain in
                    this city indefinitely. He has taken a house here. It is again published that
                    satisfactory arrangements have been made with the troops north of San Luis
                    Potosí.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
